# Store and check out all text files with LF line endings, on every OS.
# Why: Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true and would write CRLF into
# the working copy. The Linux dev container reads that working copy directly,
# and CRLF breaks bash scripts ("$'\r': command not found") and Makefile recipes.
# This file overrides the local Git setting for everyone who clones the repo.
# Binary files are detected automatically by "text=auto" and left untouched.
* text=auto eol=lf
